Infiverse_standard/src-tauri/target/

# Runtime and personal data
#
# Default deny.  Ignore the *contents* of every userdata/ directory and
# whitelist only the placeholder that keeps the directory in the tree.
#
# The previous version did the opposite: it ignored the directories and then
# re-included them with `!userdata/` so that `.gitkeep` survived.  Re-including
# a directory re-includes everything inside it, so every file the app wrote at
# runtime was committable and `git add -A` would take it without asking.  That
# is not a hypothetical: it nearly published a client secret
# (`userdata/oauth_secret_github.txt`) and then a live GitHub access token
# (`userdata/linked_accounts.json`), and the per-file patches added in response
# only ever covered the files someone happened to remember.  Denying the
# contents makes the safe answer the default, so a new runtime artifact is
# protected before anyone knows it exists.
userdata/*
!userdata/.gitkeep
Infiverse_standard/userdata/*
!Infiverse_standard/userdata/.gitkeep
Infiverse_standard/src-tauri/userdata/*
!Infiverse_standard/src-tauri/userdata/.gitkeep
# Defence in depth: these two names are credentials wherever they land, not
# only in the three directories above.
oauth_secret_*.txt
linked_accounts.json
**/messages/
**/wv2data/
*.bin
*.seed

