.zcode/
codex-reconnect-fix/
# Coordinator's own scratch: the kickoff/review prompts pasted into another
# session.  Not repository content.
.handoff/
# Leftover root from a `verse_layer_probe` run against a scratch directory.
verse_layer_probe_root/
# Per-session research scratch directory (not repository content).
# NB: this line is hygiene.  The `links` gate no longer scans untracked files at
# all (tools/check_links.py enumerates `git ls-files`), so a scratch directory
# cannot turn it red whether or not it is listed here.
.verify/
# Per-session audit scratch: probe scripts, throwaway .im files and scratch
# copies of documents kept while reviewing.  Not repository content.
# NB: this line is hygiene, not a gate dependency.  The checkers that enumerate
# repository content (tools/check_links.py, tools/check_doc_paths.py,
# tools/check_text_integrity.py) read `git ls-files`, and
# tools/check_orphan_fixtures.py globs only `vtest/` and `tools/` -- so none of
# them can see a root-level scratch directory whether or not it is listed here.
.scratch/
# Leftover root from the argument-passing / byte-declaration / range-syntax
# probes run against the engine.  Same as above: hygiene, not a gate dependency.
.probe-ie/
# Leftover from running `vtest/say_pair_probe_v06.im` by hand: line 11 calls
# `say_file("FILETEXT", "sayout.txt")` and the engine chdirs to the script's own
# directory (`chdir_to_script_dir`, src/main.c:520), so the write lands in
# `vtest/` beside the fixture rather than in the caller's cwd.  Unlike the
# entries above, this one is not a root-level scratch directory but a fixed name
# inside a tracked directory -- hence the leading slash, and hence the note
# below had to be re-derived for this path instead of copied.  No CTest runs the
# fixture (tools/check_orphan_fixtures.py records why) and the gate's fixture
# scan already runs fixtures against a *copy* of `vtest/` for this very reason
# (tools/fixture_parse.test.py), so only the hand-run case is left: nothing in
# the gate re-creates this file, which is the whole reason the line changes no
# reading.  Not repository content.
# NB: this line is hygiene, not a gate dependency.  The checkers that enumerate
# repository content read `git ls-files` (tools/check_links.py:80,
# tools/check_doc_paths.py:99, tools/check_text_integrity.py:100), and
# tools/check_orphan_fixtures.py:115 globs `vtest/*.im` -- `:55` says `*.txt` is
# not checked -- so this file cannot turn a stage red either way.
# Deliberately NOT fixed inside the fixture: the byproduct's *name* is the
# probe's observable.  The swap it guards against (docs/AUDIT.md 1.45) would
# create a file named `FILETEXT` holding `sayout.txt`, which this rule does not
# hide -- a cleanup line would have to remove that too, and that deletes the
# evidence.
/vtest/sayout.txt

# Per-session git worktrees (tools/stream.sh)
.worktrees/

# npm cache used by `npm install --cache .npm-tmp` (the default ~/.npm is not
# writable in some sessions). Build input, not source.
.npm-tmp/

